From 8ea145a63378926a2c3361b0372dea60325711a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:55:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 074/108] gpu: vulkan: pipelines linked from per-stage
 libraries, ahead-of-time pixel shader libraries

On devices with VK_EXT_graphics_pipeline_library (fast linking), extended
dynamic state 1/2/3 and dynamic rendering (Turnip; vulkan_pipeline_libraries):
- guest pipelines are linked from vertex input / pre-rasterization / fragment
  shader / fragment output libraries; cull, front face, polygon mode, depth
  clamp, rasterizer discard, depth bias enable, depth/stencil test/write/compare
  /ops and blend enable/equation/write mask are dynamic, set after binding from
  the pipeline's description (tracked, re-sent after static pipelines and at
  new command buffers);
- layouts use independent sets; per-stage library layouts are shared by every
  pair with the same texture set (thread-safe layout lookups);
- canonical interpolator masks + fixed interpolator locations so a shader's
  library doesn't depend on its pairing;
- library keys are stable across runs (ucode hash + modification, geometry
  shader key, sample state, formats) and listed in <title>.vk.libkeys once a
  saved driver cache contains them; a miss whose libraries are all known links
  synchronously (fast link, no held frame);
- first start: a background precompile builds the canonical fragment library
  of every stored pixel shader (offline-extracted set + <title>.psmeta from
  tools/lr_shader_scan.py: parameter generation register), 1x, early-Z hint and
  alpha-tested variants; marker <title>.vk.libprecompiled per driver build.
  Thor/Turnip: 8,411 libraries in 312 s (library creation is serialized by the
  driver; 4 threads = 1), warm boot loads the 334 MB driver cache in 414 ms;
- big driver caches are saved after 30 s quiet and at most every 3 minutes.
Qualcomm (no GPL/EDS3) keeps whole pipelines.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

